---Regional pricing and availability configuration for a one-time product offer.
---@class gcp.androidpublisher_v3.OneTimeProductOfferRegionalPricingAndAvailabilityConfig
---@field absoluteDiscount? gcp.androidpublisher_v3.Money The absolute value of the discount that is subtracted from the purchase option price. It should be between 0 and the purchase option price.
---@field availability? gcp.androidpublisher_v3.OneTimeProductOfferRegionalPricingAndAvailabilityConfigAvailabilityEnum|string Required. The availability for this region.
---@field regionCode? string Required. Region code this configuration applies to, as defined by ISO 3166-1 alpha-2, e.g., "US".
---@field noOverride? gcp.androidpublisher_v3.OneTimeProductOfferNoPriceOverrideOptions The price defined in the purchase option for this region will be used.
---@field relativeDiscount? number The percentage discount subtracted from the purchase option price, specified as a fraction strictly larger than `0` and strictly smaller than `1`. For example, a value of `0.8` represents an 80% discount, meaning that if the purchase option price is $100, the offer price will be $20. The resulting price will be rounded to the nearest billable unit (e.g. cents for USD). The relative discount is considered invalid if the discounted price ends up being smaller than the minimum price allowed in this region.

---@alias gcp.androidpublisher_v3.OneTimeProductOfferRegionalPricingAndAvailabilityConfigAvailabilityEnum "AVAILABILITY_UNSPECIFIED"|"AVAILABLE"|"NO_LONGER_AVAILABLE"

