---@field appLevelPermissions? gcp.androidpublisher_v3.GrantAppLevelPermissionsItemEnumList The permissions granted to the user for this app.
---@field name string Required. Resource name for this grant, following the pattern "developers/{developer}/users/{email}/grants/{package_name}". If this grant is for a draft app, the app ID will be used in this resource name instead of the package name.
---@field updateMask? string Optional. The list of fields to be updated.

---@alias gcp.androidpublisher_v3.PatchInappproductsLatencyToleranceEnum "PRODUCT_UPDATE_LATENCY_TOLERANCE_UNSPECIFIED"|"PRODUCT_UPDATE_LATENCY_TOLERANCE_LATENCY_SENSITIVE"|"PRODUCT_UPDATE_LATENCY_TOLERANCE_LATENCY_TOLERANT"

---@class gcp.androidpublisher_v3.PatchInappproductsRequest
---@field prices? gcp.androidpublisher_v3.PriceMap Prices per buyer region. None of these can be zero, as in-app products are never free. Map key is region code, as defined by ISO 3166-1 alpha-2.
---@field gracePeriod? string Deprecated: Subscriptions are no longer supported in the InAppProducts API. Use the Subscriptions API instead.
---@field defaultLanguage? string Default language of the localized data, as defined by BCP-47. e.g. "en-US".
---@field defaultPrice? gcp.androidpublisher_v3.Price Default price. Cannot be zero, as in-app products are never free. Always in the developer's Checkout merchant currency.
---@field purchaseType? gcp.androidpublisher_v3.InAppProductPurchaseTypeEnum|string The type of the product, e.g. a recurring subscription.
---@field status? gcp.androidpublisher_v3.InAppProductStatusEnum|string The status of the product, e.g. whether it's active.
---@field managedProductTaxesAndComplianceSettings? gcp.androidpublisher_v3.ManagedProductTaxAndComplianceSettings Details about taxes and legal compliance. Only applicable to managed products.
---@field trialPeriod? string Deprecated: Subscriptions are no longer supported in the InAppProducts API. Use the Subscriptions API instead.
---@field subscriptionTaxesAndComplianceSettings? gcp.androidpublisher_v3.SubscriptionTaxAndComplianceSettings Deprecated: Subscriptions are no longer supported in the InAppProducts API. Use the Subscriptions API instead.
---@field subscriptionPeriod? string Deprecated: Subscriptions are no longer supported in the InAppProducts API. Use the Subscriptions API instead.
---@field listings? gcp.androidpublisher_v3.InAppProductListingMap List of localized title and description data. Map key is the language of the localized data, as defined by BCP-47, e.g. "en-US".
---@field sku string Unique identifier for the in-app product.
---@field latencyTolerance? gcp.androidpublisher_v3.PatchInappproductsLatencyToleranceEnum|string Optional. The latency tolerance for the propagation of this product update. Defaults to latency-sensitive.
---@field packageName string Package name of the app.
---@field autoConvertMissingPrices? boolean If true the prices for all regions targeted by the parent app that don't have a price specified for this in-app product will be auto converted to the target currency based on the default price. Defaults to false.

---@alias gcp.androidpublisher_v3.PatchMonetizationOnetimeproductsLatencyToleranceEnum "PRODUCT_UPDATE_LATENCY_TOLERANCE_UNSPECIFIED"|"PRODUCT_UPDATE_LATENCY_TOLERANCE_LATENCY_SENSITIVE"|"PRODUCT_UPDATE_LATENCY_TOLERANCE_LATENCY_TOLERANT"

---@class gcp.androidpublisher_v3.PatchMonetizationOnetimeproductsRequest
---@field purchaseOptions? gcp.androidpublisher_v3.OneTimeProductPurchaseOptionList Required. The set of purchase options for this one-time product.
---@field regionsVersion? gcp.androidpublisher_v3.RegionsVersion Output only. The version of the regions configuration that was used to generate the one-time product.
---@field taxAndComplianceSettings? gcp.androidpublisher_v3.OneTimeProductTaxAndComplianceSettings Details about taxes and legal compliance.
---@field offerTags? gcp.androidpublisher_v3.OfferTagList Optional. List of up to 20 custom tags specified for this one-time product, and returned to the app through the billing library. Purchase options and offers for this product will also receive these tags in the billing library.
---@field listings? gcp.androidpublisher_v3.OneTimeProductListingList Required. Set of localized title and description data. Must not have duplicate entries with the same language_code.
---@field restrictedPaymentCountries? gcp.androidpublisher_v3.RestrictedPaymentCountries Optional. Countries where the purchase of this one-time product is restricted to payment methods registered in the same country. If empty, no payment location restrictions are imposed.
---@field updateMask? string Required. The list of fields to be updated.
---@field allowMissing? boolean Optional. If set to true, and the one-time product with the given package_name and product_id doesn't exist, the one-time product will be created. If a new one-time product is created, update_mask is ignored.
---@field packageName string Required. Immutable. Package name of the parent app.
---@field ["regionsVersion.version"]? string Required. A string representing the version of available regions being used for the specified resource. Regional prices and latest supported version for the resource have to be specified according to the information published in [this article](https://support.google.com/googleplay/android-developer/answer/10532353). Each time the supported locations substantially change, the version will be incremented. Using this field will ensure that creating and updating the resource with an older region's version and set of regional prices and currencies will succeed even though a new version is available.
---@field latencyTolerance? gcp.androidpublisher_v3.PatchMonetizationOnetimeproductsLatencyToleranceEnum|string Optional. The latency tolerance for the propagation of this product upsert. Defaults to latency-sensitive.
---@field productId string Required. Immutable. Unique product ID of the product. Unique within the parent app. Product IDs must start with a number or lowercase letter, and can contain numbers (0-9), lowercase letters (a-z), underscores (_), and periods (.).

---@alias gcp.androidpublisher_v3.PatchMonetizationSubscriptionsBasePlansOffersLatencyToleranceEnum "PRODUCT_UPDATE_LATENCY_TOLERANCE_UNSPECIFIED"|"PRODUCT_UPDATE_LATENCY_TOLERANCE_LATENCY_SENSITIVE"|"PRODUCT_UPDATE_LATENCY_TOLERANCE_LATENCY_TOLERANT"

---@class gcp.androidpublisher_v3.PatchMonetizationSubscriptionsBasePlansOffersRequest
---@field targeting? gcp.androidpublisher_v3.SubscriptionOfferTargeting The requirements that users need to fulfil to be eligible for this offer. Represents the requirements that Play will evaluate to decide whether an offer should be returned. Developers may further filter these offers themselves.
---@field regionalConfigs? gcp.androidpublisher_v3.RegionalSubscriptionOfferConfigList Required. The region-specific configuration of this offer. Must contain at least one entry.
---@field phases? gcp.androidpublisher_v3.SubscriptionOfferPhaseList Required. The phases of this subscription offer. Must contain at least one and at most two entries. Users will always receive all these phases in the specified order.
---@field state? gcp.androidpublisher_v3.SubscriptionOfferStateEnum|string Output only. The current state of this offer. Can be changed using Activate and Deactivate actions. NB: the base plan state supersedes this state, so an active offer may not be available if the base plan is not active.
---@field offerTags? gcp.androidpublisher_v3.OfferTagList List of up to 20 custom tags specified for this offer, and returned to the app through the billing library.
---@field otherRegionsConfig? gcp.androidpublisher_v3.OtherRegionsSubscriptionOfferConfig The configuration for any new locations Play may launch in the future.
---@field allowMissing? boolean Optional. If set to true, and the subscription offer with the given package_name, product_id, base_plan_id and offer_id doesn't exist, an offer will be created. If a new offer is created, update_mask is ignored.
---@field updateMask? string Required. The list of fields to be updated.
---@field basePlanId string Required. Immutable. The ID of the base plan to which this offer is an extension.
---@field packageName string Required. Immutable. The package name of the app the parent subscription belongs to.
---@field latencyTolerance? gcp.androidpublisher_v3.PatchMonetizationSubscriptionsBasePlansOffersLatencyToleranceEnum|string Optional. The latency tolerance for the propagation of this product update. Defaults to latency-sensitive.
---@field productId string Required. Immutable. The ID of the parent subscription this offer belongs to.
---@field offerId string Required. Immutable. Unique ID of this subscription offer. Must be unique within the base plan.
---@field ["regionsVersion.version"]? string Required. A string representing the version of available regions being used for the specified resource. Regional prices and latest supported version for the resource have to be specified according to the information published in [this article](https://support.google.com/googleplay/android-developer/answer/10532353). Each time the supported locations substantially change, the version will be incremented. Using this field will ensure that creating and updating the resource with an older region's version and set of regional prices and currencies will succeed even though a new version is available.

---@alias gcp.androidpublisher_v3.PatchMonetizationSubscriptionsLatencyToleranceEnum "PRODUCT_UPDATE_LATENCY_TOLERANCE_UNSPECIFIED"|"PRODUCT_UPDATE_LATENCY_TOLERANCE_LATENCY_SENSITIVE"|"PRODUCT_UPDATE_LATENCY_TOLERANCE_LATENCY_TOLERANT"

---@class gcp.androidpublisher_v3.PatchMonetizationSubscriptionsRequest
---@field archived? boolean Output only. Deprecated: subscription archiving is not supported.
---@field basePlans? gcp.androidpublisher_v3.BasePlanList The set of base plans for this subscription. Represents the prices and duration of the subscription if no other offers apply.
---@field listings? gcp.androidpublisher_v3.SubscriptionListingList Required. List of localized listings for this subscription. Must contain at least an entry for the default language of the parent app.
---@field restrictedPaymentCountries? gcp.androidpublisher_v3.RestrictedPaymentCountries Optional. Countries where the purchase of this subscription is restricted to payment methods registered in the same country. If empty, no payment location restrictions are imposed.
---@field taxAndComplianceSettings? gcp.androidpublisher_v3.SubscriptionTaxAndComplianceSettings Details about taxes and legal compliance.
---@field allowMissing? boolean Optional. If set to true, and the subscription with the given package_name and product_id doesn't exist, the subscription will be created. If a new subscription is created, update_mask is ignored.
---@field ["regionsVersion.version"]? string Required. A string representing the version of available regions being used for the specified resource. Regional prices and latest supported version for the resource have to be specified according to the information published in [this article](https://support.google.com/googleplay/android-developer/answer/10532353). Each time the supported locations substantially change, the version will be incremented. Using this field will ensure that creating and updating the resource with an older region's version and set of regional prices and currencies will succeed even though a new version is available.
---@field packageName string Immutable. Package name of the parent app.
---@field updateMask? string Required. The list of fields to be updated.
---@field productId string Immutable. Unique product ID of the product. Unique within the parent app. Product IDs must be composed of lower-case letters (a-z), numbers (0-9), underscores (_) and dots (.). It must start with a lower-case letter or number, and be between 1 and 40 (inclusive) characters in length.
---@field latencyTolerance? gcp.androidpublisher_v3.PatchMonetizationSubscriptionsLatencyToleranceEnum|string Optional. The latency tolerance for the propagation of this product update. Defaults to latency-sensitive.

---@class gcp.androidpublisher_v3.PatchUsersRequest
---@field developerAccountPermissions? gcp.androidpublisher_v3.UserDeveloperAccountPermissionsItemEnumList Permissions for the user which apply across the developer account.
---@field accessState? gcp.androidpublisher_v3.UserAccessStateEnum|string Output only. The state of the user's access to the Play Console.
---@field email? string Immutable. The user's email address.
---@field partial? boolean Output only. Whether there are more permissions for the user that are not represented here. This can happen if the caller does not have permission to manage all apps in the account. This is also `true` if this user is the account owner. If this field is `true`, it should be taken as a signal that this user cannot be fully managed via the API. That is, the API caller is not be able to manage all of the permissions this user holds, either because it doesn't know about them or because the user is the account owner.
---@field expirationTime? string The time at which the user's access expires, if set. When setting this value, it must always be in the future.
---@field grants? gcp.androidpublisher_v3.GrantList Output only. Per-app permissions for the user.
---@field name string Required. Resource name for this user, following the pattern "developers/{developer}/users/{email}".
---@field updateMask? string Optional. The list of fields to be updated.

