---A ProductPurchase resource indicates the status of a user's inapp product purchase.
---@class gcp.androidpublisher_v3.ProductPurchase
---@field purchaseTimeMillis? string The time the product was purchased, in milliseconds since the epoch (Jan 1, 1970).
---@field obfuscatedExternalAccountId? string An obfuscated version of the id that is uniquely associated with the user's account in your app. Only present if specified using https://developer.android.com/reference/com/android/billingclient/api/BillingFlowParams.Builder#setobfuscatedaccountid when the purchase was made.
---@field purchaseType? number The type of purchase of the inapp product. This field is only set if this purchase was not made using the standard in-app billing flow. Possible values are: 0. Test (i.e. purchased from a license testing account) 1. Promo (i.e. purchased using a promo code). Does not include Play Points purchases. 2. Rewarded (i.e. from watching a video ad instead of paying)
---@field obfuscatedExternalProfileId? string An obfuscated version of the id that is uniquely associated with the user's profile in your app. Only present if specified using https://developer.android.com/reference/com/android/billingclient/api/BillingFlowParams.Builder#setobfuscatedprofileid when the purchase was made.
---@field purchaseState? number The purchase state of the order. Possible values are: 0. Purchased 1. Canceled 2. Pending
---@field acknowledgementState? number The acknowledgement state of the inapp product. Possible values are: 0. Yet to be acknowledged 1. Acknowledged
---@field consumptionState? number The consumption state of the inapp product. Possible values are: 0. Yet to be consumed 1. Consumed
---@field refundableQuantity? number The quantity eligible for refund, i.e. quantity that hasn't been refunded. The value reflects quantity-based partial refunds and full refunds.
---@field developerPayload? string A developer-specified string that contains supplemental information about an order.
---@field regionCode? string ISO 3166-1 alpha-2 billing region code of the user at the time the product was granted.
---@field quantity? number The quantity associated with the purchase of the inapp product. If not present, the quantity is 1.
---@field orderId? string The order id associated with the purchase of the inapp product.
---@field productId? string The inapp product SKU. May not be present.
---@field purchaseToken? string The purchase token generated to identify this purchase. May not be present.
---@field kind? string This kind represents an inappPurchase object in the androidpublisher service.

