---@field listings? gcp.androidpublisher_v3.SubscriptionListingList Required. List of localized listings for this subscription. Must contain at least an entry for the default language of the parent app.
---@field restrictedPaymentCountries? gcp.androidpublisher_v3.RestrictedPaymentCountries Optional. Countries where the purchase of this subscription is restricted to payment methods registered in the same country. If empty, no payment location restrictions are imposed.
---@field taxAndComplianceSettings? gcp.androidpublisher_v3.SubscriptionTaxAndComplianceSettings Details about taxes and legal compliance.
---@field productId? string Immutable. Unique product ID of the product. Unique within the parent app. Product IDs must be composed of lower-case letters (a-z), numbers (0-9), underscores (_) and dots (.). It must start with a lower-case letter or number, and be between 1 and 40 (inclusive) characters in length.
---@field packageName? string Immutable. Package name of the parent app.

---A SubscriptionDeferralInfo contains the data needed to defer a subscription purchase to a future expiry time.
---@class gcp.androidpublisher_v3.SubscriptionDeferralInfo
---@field expectedExpiryTimeMillis? string The expected expiry time for the subscription. If the current expiry time for the subscription is not the value specified here, the deferral will not occur.
---@field desiredExpiryTimeMillis? string The desired next expiry time to assign to the subscription, in milliseconds since the Epoch. The given time must be later/greater than the current expiry time for the subscription.

---Details of a subscription purchase.
---@class gcp.androidpublisher_v3.SubscriptionDetails
---@field basePlanId? string The base plan ID of the subscription.
---@field servicePeriodEndTime? string The end of the billing period funded by this order. This is a snapshot of the billing/service period end time at the moment the order was processed, and should be used only for accounting. To get the current end time of the subscription service period, use purchases.subscriptionsv2.get.
---@field offerPhase? gcp.androidpublisher_v3.SubscriptionDetailsOfferPhaseEnum Deprecated: Use offer_phase_details instead. The pricing phase for the billing period funded by this order.
---@field offerPhaseDetails? gcp.androidpublisher_v3.OfferPhaseDetails The pricing phase details for the entitlement period funded by this order.
---@field servicePeriodStartTime? string The start of the billing period funded by this order. This is a snapshot of the billing/service period start time at the moment the order was processed, and should be used only for accounting.
---@field offerId? string The offer ID for the current subscription offer.

---@alias gcp.androidpublisher_v3.SubscriptionDetailsOfferPhaseEnum "OFFER_PHASE_UNSPECIFIED"|"BASE"|"INTRODUCTORY"|"FREE_TRIAL"

---Price change related information of a subscription item.
---@class gcp.androidpublisher_v3.SubscriptionItemPriceChangeDetails
---@field newPrice? gcp.androidpublisher_v3.Money New recurring price for the subscription item.
---@field priceChangeState? gcp.androidpublisher_v3.SubscriptionItemPriceChangeDetailsPriceChangeStateEnum State the price change is currently in.
---@field priceChangeMode? gcp.androidpublisher_v3.SubscriptionItemPriceChangeDetailsPriceChangeModeEnum Price change mode specifies how the subscription item price is changing.
---@field expectedNewPriceChargeTime? string The renewal time at which the price change will become effective for the user. This is subject to change(to a future time) due to cases where the renewal time shifts like pause. This field is only populated if the price change has not taken effect.

---@alias gcp.androidpublisher_v3.SubscriptionItemPriceChangeDetailsPriceChangeModeEnum "PRICE_CHANGE_MODE_UNSPECIFIED"|"PRICE_DECREASE"|"PRICE_INCREASE"|"OPT_OUT_PRICE_INCREASE"

---@alias gcp.androidpublisher_v3.SubscriptionItemPriceChangeDetailsPriceChangeStateEnum "PRICE_CHANGE_STATE_UNSPECIFIED"|"OUTSTANDING"|"CONFIRMED"|"APPLIED"|"CANCELED"

---@alias gcp.androidpublisher_v3.SubscriptionList gcp.androidpublisher_v3.Subscription[]

---The consumer-visible metadata of a subscription.
---@class gcp.androidpublisher_v3.SubscriptionListing
---@field languageCode? string Required. The language of this listing, as defined by BCP-47, e.g. "en-US".
---@field description? string The description of this subscription in the language of this listing. Maximum length - 200 characters. Plain text.
---@field benefits? gcp.androidpublisher_v3.StringList A list of benefits shown to the user on platforms such as the Play Store and in restoration flows in the language of this listing. Plain text. Ordered list of at most four benefits.
---@field title? string Required. The title of this subscription in the language of this listing. Plain text.

---@alias gcp.androidpublisher_v3.SubscriptionListingList gcp.androidpublisher_v3.SubscriptionListing[]

---A single, temporary offer
---@class gcp.androidpublisher_v3.SubscriptionOffer
---@field targeting? gcp.androidpublisher_v3.SubscriptionOfferTargeting The requirements that users need to fulfil to be eligible for this offer. Represents the requirements that Play will evaluate to decide whether an offer should be returned. Developers may further filter these offers themselves.
---@field basePlanId? string Required. Immutable. The ID of the base plan to which this offer is an extension.
---@field regionalConfigs? gcp.androidpublisher_v3.RegionalSubscriptionOfferConfigList Required. The region-specific configuration of this offer. Must contain at least one entry.
---@field phases? gcp.androidpublisher_v3.SubscriptionOfferPhaseList Required. The phases of this subscription offer. Must contain at least one and at most two entries. Users will always receive all these phases in the specified order.
---@field state? gcp.androidpublisher_v3.SubscriptionOfferStateEnum|string Output only. The current state of this offer. Can be changed using Activate and Deactivate actions. NB: the base plan state supersedes this state, so an active offer may not be available if the base plan is not active.
---@field offerId? string Required. Immutable. Unique ID of this subscription offer. Must be unique within the base plan.
---@field offerTags? gcp.androidpublisher_v3.OfferTagList List of up to 20 custom tags specified for this offer, and returned to the app through the billing library.
---@field packageName? string Required. Immutable. The package name of the app the parent subscription belongs to.
---@field otherRegionsConfig? gcp.androidpublisher_v3.OtherRegionsSubscriptionOfferConfig The configuration for any new locations Play may launch in the future.
---@field productId? string Required. Immutable. The ID of the parent subscription this offer belongs to.

---@alias gcp.androidpublisher_v3.SubscriptionOfferList gcp.androidpublisher_v3.SubscriptionOffer[]

---A single phase of a subscription offer.
---@class gcp.androidpublisher_v3.SubscriptionOfferPhase
---@field duration? string Required. The duration of a single recurrence of this phase. Specified in ISO 8601 format.
---@field recurrenceCount? number Required. The number of times this phase repeats. If this offer phase is not free, each recurrence charges the user the price of this offer phase.
---@field regionalConfigs? gcp.androidpublisher_v3.RegionalSubscriptionOfferPhaseConfigList Required. The region-specific configuration of this offer phase. This list must contain exactly one entry for each region for which the subscription offer has a regional config.
---@field otherRegionsConfig? gcp.androidpublisher_v3.OtherRegionsSubscriptionOfferPhaseConfig Pricing information for any new locations Play may launch in.

---@alias gcp.androidpublisher_v3.SubscriptionOfferPhaseList gcp.androidpublisher_v3.SubscriptionOfferPhase[]

---@alias gcp.androidpublisher_v3.SubscriptionOfferStateEnum "STATE_UNSPECIFIED"|"DRAFT"|"ACTIVE"|"INACTIVE"

---Defines the rule a user needs to satisfy to receive this offer.
---@class gcp.androidpublisher_v3.SubscriptionOfferTargeting
---@field upgradeRule? gcp.androidpublisher_v3.UpgradeTargetingRule Offer targeting rule for upgrading users' existing plans.
---@field acquisitionRule? gcp.androidpublisher_v3.AcquisitionTargetingRule Offer targeting rule for new user acquisition.

---Item-level info for a subscription purchase.
---@class gcp.androidpublisher_v3.SubscriptionPurchaseLineItem
---@field productId? string The purchased product ID (for example, 'monthly001').
---@field signupPromotion? gcp.androidpublisher_v3.SignupPromotion Promotion details about this item. Only set if a promotion was applied during signup.
---@field deferredItemRemoval? gcp.androidpublisher_v3.DeferredItemRemoval Information for deferred item removal.
---@field expiryTime? string Time at which the subscription expired or will expire unless the access is extended (ex. renews).
---@field deferredItemReplacement? gcp.androidpublisher_v3.DeferredItemReplacement Information for deferred item replacement.
---@field prepaidPlan? gcp.androidpublisher_v3.PrepaidPlan The item is prepaid.
---@field itemReplacement? gcp.androidpublisher_v3.ItemReplacement Details of the item being replaced. This field is only populated if this item replaced another item in a previous subscription and is only available for 60 days after the purchase time.
---@field offerDetails? gcp.androidpublisher_v3.OfferDetails The offer details for this item.
---@field autoRenewingPlan? gcp.androidpublisher_v3.AutoRenewingPlan The item is auto renewing.
---@field offerPhase? gcp.androidpublisher_v3.OfferPhase Current offer phase details for this item.
---@field latestSuccessfulOrderId? string The order id of the latest successful order associated with this item. Not present if the item is not owned by the user yet (e.g. the item being deferred replaced to).

---@alias gcp.androidpublisher_v3.SubscriptionPurchaseLineItemList gcp.androidpublisher_v3.SubscriptionPurchaseLineItem[]

---Indicates the status of a user's subscription purchase.
---@class gcp.androidpublisher_v3.SubscriptionPurchaseV2
---@field canceledStateContext? gcp.androidpublisher_v3.CanceledStateContext Additional context around canceled subscriptions. Only present if the subscription currently has subscription_state SUBSCRIPTION_STATE_CANCELED or SUBSCRIPTION_STATE_EXPIRED.
---@field inGracePeriodStateContext? gcp.androidpublisher_v3.InGracePeriodStateContext Optional. Additional context around subscriptions in IN_GRACE_PERIOD state. Only present if the subscription currently has subscription_state SUBSCRIPTION_STATE_IN_GRACE_PERIOD.
---@field linkedPurchaseToken? string The purchase token of the old subscription if this subscription is one of the following: * Re-signup of a canceled but non-lapsed subscription * Upgrade/downgrade from a previous subscription. * Convert from prepaid to auto renewing subscription. * Convert from an auto renewing subscription to prepaid. * Topup a prepaid subscription.
---@field externalAccountIdentifiers? gcp.androidpublisher_v3.ExternalAccountIdentifiers User account identifier in the third-party service.
---@field acknowledgementState? gcp.androidpublisher_v3.SubscriptionPurchaseV2AcknowledgementStateEnum The acknowledgement state of the subscription.
---@field regionCode? string ISO 3166-1 alpha-2 billing country/region code of the user at the time the subscription was granted.
---@field startTime? string Time at which the subscription was granted. Not set for pending subscriptions (subscription was created but awaiting payment during signup).
---@field testPurchase? gcp.androidpublisher_v3.TestPurchase Only present if this subscription purchase is a test purchase.
---@field subscribeWithGoogleInfo? gcp.androidpublisher_v3.SubscribeWithGoogleInfo User profile associated with purchases made with 'Subscribe with Google'.
---@field etag? string Entity tag representing the current state of the subscription. The developer will provide this etag for subscription actions. This etag is always present for auto-renewing and prepaid subscriptions.
---@field kind? string This kind represents a SubscriptionPurchaseV2 object in the androidpublisher service.
---@field subscriptionState? gcp.androidpublisher_v3.SubscriptionPurchaseV2SubscriptionStateEnum The current state of the subscription.
---@field onHoldStateContext? gcp.androidpublisher_v3.OnHoldStateContext Optional. Additional context around subscriptions in ON_HOLD state. Only present if the subscription currently has subscription_state SUBSCRIPTION_STATE_ON_HOLD.
---@field outOfAppPurchaseContext? gcp.androidpublisher_v3.OutOfAppPurchaseContext Additional context for out of app purchases. This information is only present for re-subscription purchases (subscription purchases made after the previous subscription of the same product has expired) made through the Google Play subscriptions center. This field will be removed after you acknowledge the subscription.
---@field pausedStateContext? gcp.androidpublisher_v3.PausedStateContext Additional context around paused subscriptions. Only present if the subscription currently has subscription_state SUBSCRIPTION_STATE_PAUSED.
---@field lineItems? gcp.androidpublisher_v3.SubscriptionPurchaseLineItemList Item-level info for a subscription purchase. The items in the same purchase should be either all with AutoRenewingPlan or all with PrepaidPlan.

---@alias gcp.androidpublisher_v3.SubscriptionPurchaseV2AcknowledgementStateEnum "ACKNOWLEDGEMENT_STATE_UNSPECIFIED"|"ACKNOWLEDGEMENT_STATE_PENDING"|"ACKNOWLEDGEMENT_STATE_ACKNOWLEDGED"

---@alias gcp.androidpublisher_v3.SubscriptionPurchaseV2SubscriptionStateEnum "SUBSCRIPTION_STATE_UNSPECIFIED"|"SUBSCRIPTION_STATE_PENDING"|"SUBSCRIPTION_STATE_ACTIVE"|"SUBSCRIPTION_STATE_PAUSED"|"SUBSCRIPTION_STATE_IN_GRACE_PERIOD"|"SUBSCRIPTION_STATE_ON_HOLD"|"SUBSCRIPTION_STATE_CANCELED"|"SUBSCRIPTION_STATE_EXPIRED"|"SUBSCRIPTION_STATE_PENDING_PURCHASE_CANCELED"

