---A user resource.
---@class gcp.androidpublisher_v3.User
---@field developerAccountPermissions? gcp.androidpublisher_v3.UserDeveloperAccountPermissionsItemEnumList Permissions for the user which apply across the developer account.
---@field name? string Required. Resource name for this user, following the pattern "developers/{developer}/users/{email}".
---@field accessState? gcp.androidpublisher_v3.UserAccessStateEnum Output only. The state of the user's access to the Play Console.
---@field email? string Immutable. The user's email address.
---@field partial? boolean Output only. Whether there are more permissions for the user that are not represented here. This can happen if the caller does not have permission to manage all apps in the account. This is also `true` if this user is the account owner. If this field is `true`, it should be taken as a signal that this user cannot be fully managed via the API. That is, the API caller is not be able to manage all of the permissions this user holds, either because it doesn't know about them or because the user is the account owner.
---@field expirationTime? string The time at which the user's access expires, if set. When setting this value, it must always be in the future.
---@field grants? gcp.androidpublisher_v3.GrantList Output only. Per-app permissions for the user.

---@alias gcp.androidpublisher_v3.UserAccessStateEnum "ACCESS_STATE_UNSPECIFIED"|"INVITED"|"INVITATION_EXPIRED"|"ACCESS_GRANTED"|"ACCESS_EXPIRED"

---User entry from conversation between user and developer.
---@class gcp.androidpublisher_v3.UserComment
---@field text? string The content of the comment, i.e. review body. In some cases users have been able to write a review with separate title and body; in those cases the title and body are concatenated and separated by a tab character.
---@field deviceMetadata? gcp.androidpublisher_v3.DeviceMetadata Information about the characteristics of the user's device.
---@field originalText? string Untranslated text of the review, where the review was translated. If the review was not translated this is left blank.
---@field starRating? number The star rating associated with the review, from 1 to 5.
---@field thumbsDownCount? number Number of users who have given this review a thumbs down.
---@field appVersionName? string String version name of the app as installed at the time the review was written. May be absent.
---@field thumbsUpCount? number Number of users who have given this review a thumbs up.
---@field device? string Codename for the reviewer's device, e.g. klte, flounder. May be absent.
---@field androidOsVersion? number Integer Android SDK version of the user's device at the time the review was written, e.g. 23 is Marshmallow. May be absent.
---@field appVersionCode? number Integer version code of the app as installed at the time the review was written. May be absent.
---@field reviewerLanguage? string Language code for the reviewer. This is taken from the device settings so is not guaranteed to match the language the review is written in. May be absent.
---@field lastModified? gcp.androidpublisher_v3.Timestamp The last time at which this comment was updated.

